From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc, eventvwr, resmon, cleanmgr, user32: our icons at every size, and a program without an icon gets ours

The administrative tools' launchers (0463) carried their icons at 16, 24,
32, 48 and 64 pixels only, so a scaled screen (125%: 20, 150%: 24, 250%:
40, large icons: 96 and 256) showed them stretched and soft. They carry
every size now, 16 to 256 pixels, each drawn for its size (sg-shell's
src/mmc/gen-icons.py through tools/sgicon.py), PNG-compressed.

theme/icons.py (run by build.sh) now also draws user32's IDI_WINLOGO (our
mark; 0441's had 16, 32, 48 and 256 pixels) and IDI_APPLICATION, the icon
of a program that has none of its own: Wine's was a wine glass, shown in
title bars and on the taskbar; ours is a plain program window under our
band, as the generic one is. Every icon icons.py draws has 16, 20, 24, 32,
40, 48, 64, 96, 128 and 256 px frames.

Test: test/iconframes-gate.sh (mutants: SG_MUTANT_ICON_FRAMES=1, and the
series without this patch: the launchers' icons have 16-64 px only).
---
--- a/programs/mmc/mmc.rc
+++ b/programs/mmc/mmc.rc
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
 /*
  * mmc.exe's icon (Stained Glass OS): the administrative consoles' own art,
  * drawn by sg-shell's src/mmc/gen-icons.py and written here as the .ico
- * file's bytes (16 to 64 pixels, PNG-compressed), so the launcher's
+ * file's bytes (16 to 256 pixels: every size a display scale asks
+ * for, each drawn for its size; PNG-compressed), so the launcher's
  * shortcuts and files show a picture, not the generic program icon.
  *
  * Copyright 2026 Stained Glass OS contributors
@@ -14,151 +15,442 @@
 
 1 ICON
